course: dictionary
lesson: 2824
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. In «Divers equalise their ears as they go down», the words going down and the ears under water show that a diver is a person who swims underwater.
explain: The same word can mean something else. In «A diver leapt from the high board and cut into the pool», the board and the splash show the sport of jumping into water. A diver can also be a water bird, called a loon in North America.
explain: Ask yourself what is happening in the sentence. Is someone using breathing equipment, going deeper, or rescuing someone? Or is someone jumping off a board? Then put your chosen meaning into the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: A diver is a person who swims underwater, often with special breathing equipment, to explore, work or rescue.
fact: A diver can also be a person who jumps into water from a board as a sport, like a «high diver».
fact: A diver can also be a diving water bird, called a loon in North America.
fact: «Scuba diver» and «deep-sea diver» are phrases for divers who go underwater with special equipment.
fact: «Divers equalise their ears» means they even out the push inside their ears as they go down, for example by pinching the nose and blowing gently.
exercise: «Divers equalise their ears as they go down.» In this sentence, what is a diver? | A ship that sails on the sea | *A person who swims underwater with breathing equipment | A bird that dives for fish | A person who jumps off a high board
exercise: «The high diver leapt from the board and cut into the pool with barely a splash.» Which meaning of diver is used? | A fish with venomous spines | A person who swims underwater to explore wrecks | A water bird that hunts fish | *A person who jumps into water from a board as a sport
exercise: «Lionfish have venomous spines; divers hunt them to help reefs.» Why do divers hunt lionfish? | Because lionfish are a kind of diving bird | *Because lionfish have spread far from their home seas and harm reefs | Because lionfish make the best pets | Because lionfish can fly
test: «The sperm whale's clicks could hurt a diver very close by.» In this sentence, a diver means: | A small boat | A person who jumps from a board | A bird that dives for fish | *A person who swims underwater
test: Which phrase describes a diver who goes down in the sea with special breathing equipment? | high diver | *scuba diver | diving board | diver's ears
exam: «Divers come up slowly, because shooting up fast can badly hurt them.» Why do divers come up slowly? | Because they are tired of swimming | *Because shooting up fast can badly hurt them | Because the bird is watching them | Because the sea is too cold to swim in quickly
